  "prefLabel": "Gal 301.06 Permanency hearing",
  "priorExpiration": "2016-10-15",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Gal 301.06 “Permanency hearing” means a judicial hearing that takes place after a child has been placed out of his or her regular home for an extended period of time, the purpose of which is to determine the child’s permanent living arrangement.\n\nSource. #8101, eff 1-1-05; ss by #8942, eff 9-15-07, EXPIRED: 9-15-15\n\nNew. #11075, INTERIM, eff 4-18-16, EXPIRED: 10-15-16\n\nNew. #12010, eff 10-21-16",
